From 9d1513030c8bde38d62b64165a7fef965757899b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Russell Ballestrini <russell@unturf.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/29] b43: AC-PHY TX header with TOE prefix, and the core rev >= 40 TX status

ucode 907 (core rev 40/42, PHY type AC) takes a different TX header and
returns a different TX status than the 598 format b43 knows.

TX header: wl.ko wlc_d11hdrs @0x11b360 builds a 124 byte header for PHY
type 11 (cmp r3, #11 at 0x11b384): 20 byte packet part, four 20 byte
rate entries, 24 byte tail. b43 sends legacy CCK/OFDM at 20 MHz, so the
header is the one wl writes for a frame outside its rate selection: one
rate entry, MAC control high word 0x0002, chanspec, 802.11 header length,
frame length + FCS, frame id, sequence control, PHY control 0 and 2
(wlc_acphy_txctl0_calc @0x1135a0, wlc_acphy_txctl2_calc @0x114a24), PLCP,
rate, last-entry bit. On core rev > 39 wl puts a 4 byte TOE prefix
{0x02, 0, 0, 0} in front of it (wlc_toe_add_hdr 0x199ef4, enabled at
wlc_attach 0x13d4fc) and wlc_up clears MMIO 0xa00 bit 0 (0x129bdc); the
hardware takes the first 4 bytes of every TX buffer as that prefix
(wlc_get_txh_info skips them, 0x2d50..0x2d78). Without the prefix
every TX status came back with frame id 0 and sequence 0. The header
becomes 128 bytes and the PIO scratch space grows to match.

Frame id: with the AC header the DMA cookie uses wl's layout, FIFO in
bits 0..2 and the slot in bits 5..14 (0x11b734..0x11b744).

TX status: core rev >= 40 reads two four-word packages from 0x170..0x17c
in wl's order (wlc_bmac_txstatus @0x12270, rev > 39 branch at 0x12288),
drops the status when the second package lacks its valid bit, and maps
acked, intermediate, pm, suppress reason, frame and RTS counts.

Hardware crypto is refused on the AC header (the key bytes and the 907
key table are not decoded), so mac80211 encrypts in software. The 598,
410 and 351 paths are unchanged.
